asis"],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1994-03-25","later-events_catalog":"1994-03-25","stage19_causal_queue":"1994-03-25","stage21_crosswalk":"1994-03-25"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:12905","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Source: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9\nLocation: 59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; operative words before the numbered sections","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#preamble-op","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Establishment There is established in the Office of the United  \nStates Trade Representative (“Trade Representative” the “Trade and Environ­\nm ent Policy A dvisory Com m ittee” (“ Com m ittee”).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; Sec. 1","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Com m ittee shall consist of not m ore than  \n35 m em bers, including, but not lim ited to, representatives from environ­\nm ental interest groups, industry (including the environm ental technology  \n_  and environm ental services industries), agriculture, services, non-Federal\ngovernm ent, and consum er interests. The Com m ittee should be broadly rep­\nresentative of the key sectors and groups of the econom y w ith an interest  \nin trade and environm ental policy issues.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Chairm an of the Comm ittee shall be elected by the Committee  \nfrom among its members. Members o f the Com m ittee shall be appointed  \nby the Trade Representative, in consultation w ith the Cabinet secretaries  \ndescribed in section 2155(c)(1) of title 19, U nited States Code, for a term  \nof 2 years and m ay be reappointed for any num ber of term s. Appointm ents  \nto the Com m ittee shall be m ade w ithout regard to political affiliation. Any  \nm em ber m ay be rem oved at the discretion of the Trade Representative.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3 . Functions, [a) The Comm ittee shall provide the Trade Representative  \nw ith policy advice on issues involving trade and the environm ent.\n(b) T he Com m ittee shall submit a report to the President, to the Congress,  \nand to the Trade Representative at the conclusion of negotiations for each  \ntrade agreem ent referred to in section 102 of the A ct. The report shall  \ninclude an advisory opinion on w hether and to w hat extent the agreement  \nprom otes the interests of the United States.\n(c) The Com m ittee may establish such subcom m ittees of its members  \nas it deem s necessary, subject to the provisions of the Federal Advisory  \nCom m ittee A ct and the approval of the Trade Representative, or his designee.\n(d) The Com m ittee shall report its activities to the Trade Representative,  \nor his designee.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; Sec. 3","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Trade Representative, or his designee, with  \nthe advice of the Chairm an, shall be responsible for prior approval o f the  \nagendas for all Com m ittee meetings.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Trade Representative, or his designee, shall be responsible for  \ndeterm inations, filings, and other adm inistrative requirem ents of the Federal  \nA dvisory Com m ittee A ct.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) (1) The Trade Representative shall provide funding and adm inistrative  \nand staff support for the Committee.\n(2) The Com m ittee shall have an Executive D irector who shall be a  \nFederal officer or em ployee designated by the Trade Representative.\n\n=== PDF page 204 of 212 ===","original_source":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204; Sec. 4(c)","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12905#sec4(c)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"59 FR 14733, PDF pages 203-204","sha256":"bd81c66be003f77c3f43ebca340c1e9fb8940437fcaa8afe48550a5f21fe29b9","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1994-03-29/pdf/FR-1994-03-29.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 8 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: current legal basis not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"yes"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12905"}
